Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["From a Sullivan Model to an IBL Algebra", "Title",
 CellID->509267359,ExpressionUUID->"4ddb5767-1f00-4973-a411-49eacd07850d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The dIBL algebra of a closed oriented ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "68a7c88e-0033-4312-820f-56a7ed9efb28"],
 "-manifold ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b1d13cd-3a94-459f-bb74-77fabd3d3563"],
 " lives on the cyclic words of a graded alphabet, and the alphabet is a \
basis of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], "*"], "(", 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "200cc4a8-e50f-479a-9e1e-4728604fc797"],
 " shifted by one, with the pairing that Poincar\[EAcute] duality gives it. \
This tutorial builds that alphabet without ever mentioning ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2797a08a-5522-4b9a-8d8b-909f9e64e0d1"],
 ": it starts from a Sullivan minimal model, puts the natural orientation on \
it, checks that the resulting oriented PDGA is of Hodge type, passes to the \
nondegenerate quotient, and reads the canonical Maurer-Cartan element off the \
triple product of the quotient. The running example is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["CP",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4a8f7dd8-f724-4c50-a51b-ac98bc942eec"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2d83f16a-3ffe-489f-8c60-0ae189945878"],

Cell["Five steps, and each one is a single function.", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5732df93-90a8-4c47-99a5-7762b30e3102"],

Cell["The minimal model", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"deaed7ff-fcd1-4d70-8a35-064e62f88204"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A Sullivan minimal model is a free graded commutative algebra ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalLambda]", 
    StyleBox["U", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bbd425f5-12c3-48d6-8b1b-7b89c74d8a5e"],
 " with a differential. For ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["CP",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ee183ca0-6fa5-46ca-95cb-c8782f17848b"],
 " it has two generators: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f349a103-a780-411d-9c5e-9d479ad01028"],
 " in degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["2", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f0c8ed8-d935-4641-8720-56cec6b0cfe2"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9fde39eb-1a78-43d8-aea0-d50219c4427c"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["b", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1f808d26-075e-40cc-b7ff-41ce8cca28eb"],
 " in degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"2", 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"], "+", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2a350c2a-5c7e-438c-a79d-997ee8405cc4"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["m", "TI"], "+", "1"}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "27ccf781-e2b6-4b76-94cb-cca1df53b0f3"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cc82c67f-0fdf-4a96-8e60-58aff026946b"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"model", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"SullivanModel", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<ComplexProjectiveSpace\>\"", "[", "2", "]"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
  RowBox[{"model", "[", "\"\<Generators\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"ed8ea609-c3fe-45bc-bc9b-25a94a329744"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"a", "\[Rule]", "2"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"b", "\[Rule]", "5"}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[1]= ",ExpressionUUID->"a263224c-7bfa-4a36-858d-6658fba4a4ae"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
The differential is stored on the generators and extended as a derivation. It \
raises degree by one:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6e647712-db5d-45e9-b35a-07216caf9f06"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"SullivanModelDifferential", "[", 
    RowBox[{"b", ",", " ", "model"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"SullivanModelDifferential", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"a", " ", "b"}], ",", " ", "model"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"499a71f1-9c80-4f35-92c6-d3b6f7fa203a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["a", "3"], ",", 
   SuperscriptBox["a", "4"]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[2]= ",ExpressionUUID->"a78ad01b-7a11-4739-acaa-02e5a2af7a75"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A monomial is written as a product of generators, read in the order the \
model declares them. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["SullivanModelBasis"]], 
    "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/SullivanModelBasis", "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "9ebfc160-d1d5-4dca-b98b-57efd23cdeec"],
 " lists the monomials of one degree; the algebra is infinite-dimensional, \
one or two monomials in every degree from here up."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9e4aa073-171a-47ab-bf27-cbf5e8c59017"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"SullivanModelBasis", "[", 
    RowBox[{"model", ",", " ", "k"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "8"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[3]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"6a0f8014-39be-4799-affd-d55658d70663"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "1", "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", "a", "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    SuperscriptBox["a", "2"], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", "b", "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    SuperscriptBox["a", "3"], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"a", " ", "b"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    SuperscriptBox["a", "4"], "}"}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[3]= ",ExpressionUUID->"4a501b1b-f7aa-4db3-8936-e12772550c40"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["The orientation, and the pairing it defines", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"c3a1e3c2-3e27-4fe9-b083-daa52eea9383"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The cohomology of this model is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["R",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{"[", 
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "]"}], "/", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["a", "TI"], "3"], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "75839df1-d146-43bd-8174-3cacc90544f1"],
 ", so the top class is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "2"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "117ebbf8-1800-46a7-8345-613644fb7853"],
 " in degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["4", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cc59ad5a-ee8a-4910-8415-caa37b32bbad"],
 ". Let the orientation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "00eb9bc2-3eeb-490d-bf5f-a4f3066f796d"],
 " be the coefficient of that monomial: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["1", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "32bcc732-a137-4295-8a4a-5d0c70c9a338"],
 " on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "2"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ce7c5cd5-5950-4ab0-a116-1e6215ddd910"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["0", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "47fb6b9e-be65-490a-8d1f-c80ec7f290a5"],
 " on everything else. That is what ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"model", "[", "\"\<Orientation\>\"", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b5d2beb8-9876-487b-9dd7-fd6beb45c58b"],
 " records, as its values on the monomials of degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["4", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f0563f97-6c5a-4a96-b149-eeb188becec7"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f567b6ee-2eb2-4d69-ae34-119975b8b6be"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"model", "[", "\"\<Orientation\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"model", "[", "\"\<Degree\>\"", "]"}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"c8c491c9-1675-4532-8f7d-8e4c1f4da179"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["a", "2"], "\[Rule]", "1"}], "\[RightAssociation]"}], ",",
    "4"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[4]= ",ExpressionUUID->"375b2b3e-a731-4d9c-8f20-5cba89887443"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["SullivanModelOrientation"]], 
    "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/SullivanModelOrientation", 
    "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "f17c89bb-aaf2-44fc-a890-833eda46213d"],
 " applies it. Everything outside degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["4", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3e30ded0-2391-4f4c-8eb9-32ee9d7550df"],
 " is killed, and inside degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["4", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9c0862dd-1265-4cb7-b93a-7b6509db4ea6"],
 " only ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "2"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d8d895f3-0d08-4eb7-a41b-6a6c7b4dd4eb"],
 " survives:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ffcc03b6-6701-4b46-9226-391caecde8c9"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"SullivanModelOrientation", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"a", "^", "2"}], ",", " ", "model"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"SullivanModelOrientation", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"a", "^", "3"}], ",", " ", "model"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"SullivanModelOrientation", "[", 
    RowBox[{"b", ",", " ", "model"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[5]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"0bfe0b33-f367-4120-9659-52d73d528902"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"1", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[5]= ",ExpressionUUID->"5714ab28-aab5-4ce5-bc6e-69dc9ea8ab0a"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The pairing is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[LeftAngleBracket]", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["v", "TI"], "1"], ",", 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["v", "TI"], "2"]}], "\[RightAngleBracket]"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
    
    StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["v", "TI"], "1"], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["v", "TI"], "2"]}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4d033474-9e7e-44d4-86a8-1e3888a0d41e"],
 ", the orientation of the product. On ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"1", ",", 
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], ",", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "2"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3a5b5bd8-cdd6-4e12-bbad-0115dc9f6ebe"],
 " it is the antidiagonal, which is Poincar\[EAcute] duality:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ff8b651f-908e-4ef3-b391-a620de393616"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"SullivanModelPairing", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"a", "^", "i"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"a", "^", "j"}], ",", " ", "model"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"i", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"j", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", "//", 
  " ", "MatrixForm"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[6]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"90459994-6185-4ed8-9f79-873bfd1d59b8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  RowBox[{"(", "\[NoBreak]", GridBox[{
     {"0", "0", "1"},
     {"0", "1", "0"},
     {"1", "0", "0"}
    },
    GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Center}}, "Rows" -> {{Baseline}}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {
        Offset[0.27999999999999997`], {
         Offset[0.7]}, 
        Offset[0.27999999999999997`]}, "Rows" -> {
        Offset[0.2], {
         Offset[0.4]}, 
        Offset[0.2]}}], "\[NoBreak]", ")"}],
  Function[BoxForm`e$, 
   MatrixForm[BoxForm`e$]]]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[6]= ",ExpressionUUID->"3f58584c-b1d9-4d61-8987-b66757cc0bb3"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This is an ",
 StyleBox["orientation", "TI"],
 " in the sense of Lambrechts-Stanley: it has degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["4", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "22ce174a-c3c1-43a1-9c2e-42f7f1407359"],
 ", it kills the image of the differential, and it does not vanish on the \
kernel. Together with the perfect pairing it induces on cohomology, that \
makes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"\[CapitalLambda]", 
     StyleBox["U", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["d",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], ",", 
     StyleBox["O", "TI"]}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "221438ab-5035-43e9-a5b8-ab343d9b6cfa"],
 " an oriented PDGA of degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["4", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d8ca6567-0f8d-43eb-b7cc-493dae02e9a6"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4274833f-4530-4edd-abab-7ae6303eb85d"],

Cell["Is it of Hodge type?", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"eca75cb5-62bf-451f-822e-dc5c31a6ae55"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The pairing is ",
 StyleBox["not", "TI"],
 " perfect on chain level: the whole of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalLambda]", 
    StyleBox["U", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ba16d7bc-4d88-4dcd-ba32-e0ac03a10e38"],
 " above degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["4", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "668898bb-adb0-4f4a-bcbd-eec5dea8dd19"],
 " is paired to zero with everything, because the orientation only sees \
degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["4", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7de447c0-1478-45e7-a94d-c4e5581f4aa4"],
 ". Those elements form the ",
 StyleBox["degenerate subspace", "TI"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["deg",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "24ff70d7-3172-4373-928d-d625bb7d595b"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cbd9b202-8a25-4996-8890-56de749b70da"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"DegenerateSubspace", "[", 
    RowBox[{"model", ",", " ", "5"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"DegenerateSubspace", "[", 
    RowBox[{"model", ",", " ", "6"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"DegenerateSubspace", "[", 
    RowBox[{"model", ",", " ", "7"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[7]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"1dc5b020-c7af-452a-aaf7-6b1a1e7b4377"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "b", "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    SuperscriptBox["a", "3"], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"a", " ", "b"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[7]= ",ExpressionUUID->"ea6100f3-bf32-44f0-85a5-460312db75b1"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The oriented PDGA is ",
 StyleBox["of Hodge type", "TI"],
 " when it admits a Hodge decomposition ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    StyleBox["H", "TI"], "\[CirclePlus]", 
    StyleBox["im",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
    StyleBox["d",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[CirclePlus]", 
    StyleBox["C", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "26377c01-2c4d-4612-946a-4d8c1d2c463b"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["C", "TI"], "\[Perpendicular]", 
    StyleBox["C", "TI"], "\[CirclePlus]", 
    StyleBox["H", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5c9eaf02-a55b-4563-8749-101677583455"],
 ". Over a field of characteristic ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[NotEqual]", "2"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "60f3f663-b65d-412e-b563-c2f2d6ceda1f"],
 " and for a quotient of finite type, that happens exactly when ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["deg",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "684f9fb2-d3d1-4b92-b4ac-891c6db4bd0b"],
 " is acyclic, equivalently exactly when the quotient map onto the \
nondegenerate quotient is a quasi-isomorphism. So the test is one cohomology \
computation."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"100b6612-743d-410a-847f-02c192cdc139"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"HodgeTypeQ", "[", "model", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[8]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"d9b45a71-f34e-4aee-bafd-ed77849bc920"],

Cell[BoxData["True"], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[8]= ",ExpressionUUID->"46c4718b-8275-436d-85ab-65786d7cc4d5"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["HodgeTypeReport"]], "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/HodgeTypeReport", 
    "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "6bdb7618-2bd8-4022-b11c-7b4a9096f8e2"],
 " shows why, degree by degree. The fourth column is the cohomology of the \
degenerate subspace, and it vanishes throughout. Here the second and fifth \
columns agree as well, which says more: the quotient carries no differential, \
so it ",
 StyleBox["is", "TI"],
 " the cohomology: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["CP",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "64f6d1dc-2bb4-45e6-80c5-bb709769a202"],
 " is formal. A Hodge-type model whose quotient keeps a differential has ",
 Cell[BoxData["Cohomology"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e66759f7-1e94-45c6-a81a-077f7f4176e3"],
 " strictly below ",
 Cell[BoxData["Quotient"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ec3a0b0-fc16-4dee-9558-7764e760a6fd"],
 ", and the next tutorial shows one."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2906940e-9045-41b2-b192-bc48eb2348a8"],

